{
    "about": [
        "Coefficients of friction by pair of materials, for a contact set whose",
        "FrictionFrom is Materials (docs/AssemblyDynamics.md, P6). A component's",
        "material card is in the first family one of whose words its name, its",
        "KindOfMaterial or one of its tags holds, ignoring case; a component with",
        "no card, or one in no family, and a pair not listed here, run on the set's",
        "own StaticFriction and DynamicFriction. A card's name is the Material",
        "manager's, its file's: PA6-Generic, not the Polyamide 6 inside it.",
        "One scale: clean and dry, in air, all from the one source, so that one",
        "pair stands against another -- steel on steel above nylon on steel, as",
        "it is. Where the source gives two coefficients they are the static and",
        "the dynamic; where it gives one it is the static one, and the dynamic is",
        "five sixths of it, the source's own steel on steel (0.42 / 0.50); where",
        "it gives a range, or two rows, its low end. Restitution stays the set's:",
        "it depends on the speed more than on the pair.",
        "A file of the same form at <user data>/Assembly/ContactFriction.json is",
        "read over this one: its families are tried first, its pairs replace these."
    ],
    "sources": {
        "toolbox": "The Engineering ToolBox, 'Friction - Coefficients for Common Materials and Surfaces' (2004): clean and dry (read 2026-11-03)"
